# ── Cx4: the snes9x reference, DELIBERATELY UNTRACKED ─────────────────────
# The SHIPPING Cx4 (runner/src/snes/cx4.c) is an instruction-level HG51B S169
# core ported from ares, which is ISC-licensed — permissive, notice-only — so it
# IS committed.
#
# These *.reference files are the earlier snes9x-derived command-level model,
# kept locally only as a cross-check while validating the ares port. The Snes9x
# license is freeware / NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY, so committing them would put that
# constraint into this repo's public history permanently. They are not compiled.
# Delete them once the ares core is validated.
runner/src/snes/*.reference

# Cx4 internal data ROM: Capcom/Hitachi firmware, user-supplied. Never commit.
# All three names are the same 3072-byte blob (sha256 ae8d4d19...): `cx4.rom` is
# ares' firmware-directory name, `hg51bs169.data.rom` is its gamepak name, and
# `cx4.data.rom` is what the common firmware sets ship it as.
cx4.rom
cx4.data.rom
hg51bs169.data.rom

# DSP-1 / DSP-1B firmware: Nintendo/NEC firmware, user-supplied. Never commit.
dsp1.rom
dsp1b.rom
dsp1.bin
/build-data-packs/
